# Path ignores for the opengrep SAST scan in .github/workflows/scan.yaml.
#
# ASCII ONLY: opengrep's ignore-file parser (semgrep/ignores.py) decodes this file as ASCII and
# exits 2 on any other byte, which kills the whole scan stage. No em dashes, no curly quotes.
#
# This file REPLACES opengrep's built-in default ignore list, so that list is restated first.
# Dropping it is how test/ (never scanned by default) once produced sixty-odd alerts in one run.
:include .gitignore
.git/
node_modules/
build/
dist/
vendor/
.env/
.venv/
.tox/
*.min.js
test/
tests/
*_test.go
.semgrep
.semgrep_logs

# Prose and generated reports. Several registry rules are bare regexes over raw bytes: the
# insecure-websocket rule matches the plain "ws" URL scheme anywhere but localhost, in comments,
# in documentation, and in this file itself if it were spelled out here. That scheme is accepted
# by design (src/config/core-settings.ts, NODE), so every mention in prose is a false positive.
# Code stays scanned; a flagged code line carries a `nosemgrep: <rule-id>` marker instead, which
# keeps the finding out of the scanner's own report. The SARIF sent to GitHub code scanning still
# lists marked findings (with suppressions: inSource, which GitHub ignores), so each marked or
# prose line also needs its GitHub alert dismissed once; see docs/issues/00086 for the action-level
# fix that would end that.
*.md
graphify-out/
